(183016, 'False', 57, '2026-03-23 00:00:00', 10, 'DR. LEAH J. BUENDIA', 480, 'Engr. Ninaliza H. Escorial', 'PCIEERD 26-548\r\nNICER: ACCELERATING SALT RESEARCH AND INNOVATION CENTER (ASIN CENTER)\r\n\r\nProject 2. Establishment of Asin R&D Center through Technology, Competence, and Services Development', 'Refers to the extended DOST-GIA funded project entitled \"Project 2. Establishment of Asin R&D Center through Technology, Competence, and Services Development\". Please be informed that the Council approved the request of the Pangasinan State University For the 2nd Extension of the said project from 16 March 2026 - 15 June 2026 (3 months) to complete the fabrication and installation of the Spray Pipe and Mesh Net Technology for the Seawater Evaporation System.\r\nOne of the technologies of this project which is very critical and important as it offers salt farmers an alternative solution for producing salt even in limited spaces of without access to traditional solar saltern farms.', 6, NULL, 26, 'forwarded hardcopy to Lem. 03/23/2026', 1644, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 1, 'False', '2026-07-09 06:58:52', NULL, '2026-07-09 06:58:52', 1, '2026-07-09 06:58:52', 1),
(183017, 'False', 57, '2026-03-23 00:00:00', 38, 'Dr. Annabelle V. Briones', 39, 'Engr. Robert O. Dizon', 'Retrofitting of the DOST Water Retort for Improved Functionality and Performance. ', 'Refers to letter dated 27 February 2026 regarding the implementation of GAA-funded research project entitled \"Retrofitting of the DOST Water Retort for Improved Functionality and Performance. \" The center has no objection to the proposed retrofitting of the DOST-developed Modular Water Retort unit currently stationed at DOST-ITDI. However, as the equipment remains the property of the DOST, the funding agency of the original project entitled \"Rollout of DOST-developed Food Processing Equipment for the Regions\" and given that the activity involves modifications to its design and configuration, approval from DOST-SPD should be secured before proceeding with the retrofitting. ', 6, NULL, 75, 'forwarded hardcopy to Boyet 03/23/2026', 1644, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 1, 'False', '2026-07-09 06:58:52', NULL, '2026-07-09 06:58:52', 1, '2026-07-09 06:58:52', 1),
(183018, 'False', 57, '2026-03-23 00:00:00', 39, 'Engr. Robert O. Dizon', 480, 'Engr. Ninaliza H. Escorial', 'PCIEERD 26-00552\r\nSTRUCTUR3D: Structural Resilience and Utility of 3D-Printed Load-Bearing Structure in the Philippines', 'Reference to the letter dated 12 February 2026 received on 18 February 2026 requesting a change in start date of the DOST-GIA funded project titled \"STRUCTUR3D: Structural Resilience and Utility of 3D-Printed Load-Bearing Structure in the Philippines\" PCIEERD approved the above request, taking into consideration the justification provided, particularly that the project had already initiated the hiring pf personnel as early as January 2026, and project activities has commenced. However, that the date falls beyond the 3 month period from the actual release of funds which was on 24 September 2025. The NCA meanwhile, was only issued on 09 February 2026. The start date is 1 month ahead of the NCA issuance, but within the date stipulated in the notarized MOA. The new implementation period of the project in 01 January 2026-31 December 2027, any expenses incurred before January 01 2026 are not allowed. ', 6, NULL, 26, 'forwarded harcopy to Armela. 03/23/2026\r\n(cc only)', 1644, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 1, 'False', '2026-07-09 06:58:52', NULL, '2026-07-09 06:58:52', 1, '2026-07-09 06:58:52', 1),
